@@ -0,0 +1,207 @@
+MusicBrainz
+===========
+
+Search, look up and browse `MusicBrainz <https://musicbrainz.org>`_, the open music encyclopedia,
+and prepare releases for submission to it.
+
+The block talks to the `MusicBrainz web service (WS/2) <https://musicbrainz.org/doc/MusicBrainz_API>`_
+directly from the browser and follows the MusicBrainz
+`rate limiting rules <https://musicbrainz.org/doc/MusicBrainz_API/Rate_Limiting>`_:
+
+- Every request carries a ``User-Agent`` of the form ``KendraioApp/<version> ( https://github.com/kendraio/kendraio-app )``.
+  MusicBrainz allows this header in its CORS policy. Browsers that do not let pages set it (Chromium-based browsers)
+  send their own User-Agent and the page Origin instead.
+- All MusicBrainz blocks in the app share one request queue that sends at most one request per second.
+  Requests that MusicBrainz throttles (HTTP 503 or 429) are retried with back-off.
+- Identical requests are only sent once: responses are cached for five minutes, and two blocks asking for the same
+  thing at the same time share one request.
+
+Default config
+--------------
+
+.. code-block:: json
+
+    {
+      "type": "musicbrainz",
+      "operation": "search",
+      "entity": "artist",
+      "limit": 25,
+      "resultsOnly": true,
+      "valueGetters": {
+        "query": "data.query"
+      }
+    }
+
+Supported properties
+--------------------
+
+- **operation** - ``search`` (default), ``lookup``, ``browse`` or ``seed-release``. See below.
+- **entity** - The MusicBrainz entity type, e.g. ``artist`` (default), ``release``, ``release-group``, ``recording``,
+  ``label``, ``work``, ``area``, ``event``, ``instrument``, ``place``, ``series``, ``url``.
+- **query** - ``search`` only. A `search query <https://musicbrainz.org/doc/MusicBrainz_API/Search>`_ string
+  (e.g. ``artist:Björk AND country:IS``) or an object of field/value pairs, e.g. ``{"artist": "Björk", "country": "IS"}``.
+  Object fields are AND-ed together, array values are OR-ed, empty values are ignored and values are quoted, so the
+  output of a form can be used directly.
+- **dismax** (boolean) - ``search`` only. Use the simpler "dismax" query parser for free text queries.
+- **mbid** - ``lookup`` only. The MusicBrainz identifier (MBID) of the entity.
+- **linkedEntity** and **linkedMbid** - ``browse`` only. List the entities linked to another entity, e.g. the
+  ``release-group`` entities of an ``artist``. The block reports an error if the combination is not supported by MusicBrainz.
+- **inc** - ``lookup`` and ``browse``. Extra data to include, as an array or a ``+`` separated string,
+  e.g. ``["aliases", "genres", "url-rels"]``. Unsupported values are reported before anything is sent.
+- **releaseType** and **releaseStatus** - Filter releases and release groups, e.g. ``["album", "ep"]`` and ``official``.
+- **limit** (1-100) and **offset** - Paging for ``search`` and ``browse``.
+- **resultsOnly** (boolean, default false) - Output only the list of results (e.g. the ``artists`` array of an artist search)
+  instead of the whole response, ready for a Grid block.
+- **valueGetters** - JMESPath expressions that compute any of the properties above from the incoming ``data`` or
+  the Flow ``context``, e.g. ``{"mbid": "context.queryParams.mbid"}``.
+- **skipInit** (boolean, default true) - Do not run on the initial, empty input of the Flow.
+- **apiRoot** - Web service root. Defaults to ``https://musicbrainz.org/ws/2``; use ``https://test.musicbrainz.org/ws/2``
+  or a mirror for testing.
+- **userAgent** - Override the User-Agent, e.g. to identify a Flow you publish: ``MyLabelCatalogue/1.0 ( me@example.com )``.
+- **sendUserAgent** (boolean, default true) - Set to false to not send the User-Agent header.
+- **minIntervalMs** (default 1000) - Minimum delay between requests. It can be raised but not lowered below 1000 for musicbrainz.org.
+- **maxRetries** (default 2) - How often a throttled request is retried.
+- **cacheTtlMs** (default 300000) - How long responses are cached. ``0`` disables the cache for this block.
+
+The block does nothing until it has something to ask: an empty search or a missing MBID is not sent.
+Errors (invalid MBIDs, unsupported ``inc`` values, MusicBrainz errors) are shown in the block.
+
+Search
+------
+
+Search for artists using the fields of a form:
+
+.. code-block:: json
+
+    [
+      {
+        "type": "form",
+        "jsonSchema": {
+          "type": "object",
+          "properties": {
+            "artist": { "type": "string", "title": "Artist name" },
+            "country": { "type": "string", "title": "Country code" }
+          }
+        },
+        "uiSchema": {}
+      },
+      {
+        "type": "musicbrainz",
+        "operation": "search",
+        "entity": "artist",
+        "limit": 50,
+        "resultsOnly": true,
+        "valueGetters": { "query": "data" }
+      },
+      {
+        "type": "grid",
+        "columnDefs": [
+          { "headerName": "Name", "field": "name" },
+          { "headerName": "Country", "field": "country" },
+          { "headerName": "Score", "field": "score" }
+        ]
+      }
+    ]
+
+Lookup
+------
+
+Look up the artist whose MBID is in the ``mbid`` query parameter of the page (``/musicbrainz/artist?mbid=...``):
+
+.. code-block:: json
+
+    {
+      "type": "musicbrainz",
+      "operation": "lookup",
+      "entity": "artist",
+      "inc": ["aliases", "genres", "url-rels"],
+      "valueGetters": { "mbid": "context.queryParams.mbid" }
+    }
+
+Browse
+------
+
+List the albums and EPs of an artist:
+
+.. code-block:: json
+
+    {
+      "type": "musicbrainz",
+      "operation": "browse",
+      "entity": "release-group",
+      "linkedEntity": "artist",
+      "releaseType": ["album", "ep"],
+      "limit": 100,
+      "resultsOnly": true,
+      "valueGetters": { "linkedMbid": "data.id" }
+    }
+
+Submitting a release (release editor seeding)
+---------------------------------------------
+
+MusicBrainz does not accept new releases through its web service. Instead, applications
+`seed the release editor <https://wiki.musicbrainz.org/Development/Release_Editor_Seeding>`_: the release details are
+POSTed to the MusicBrainz website, which opens its release editor with them filled in, so the user can check, complete
+and submit them under their own MusicBrainz account.
+
+With ``"operation": "seed-release"`` the block turns the incoming data (or the result of ``valueGetters.release``) into
+the release editor fields and shows a button that opens the editor in a new tab. The block also outputs
+``{"action": "<editor URL>", "fields": [{"name": "...", "value": "..."}]}``.
+
+.. code-block:: json
+
+    {
+      "type": "musicbrainz",
+      "operation": "seed-release",
+      "label": "Open in MusicBrainz release editor",
+      "siteRoot": "https://test.musicbrainz.org"
+    }
+
+``siteRoot`` defaults to ``https://musicbrainz.org``; use ``https://test.musicbrainz.org`` while trying things out.
+The release data has this shape (only ``name`` is required):
+
+.. code-block:: json
+
+    {
+      "name": "Night Drive",
+      "type": "ep",
+      "status": "official",
+      "barcode": "",
+      "artistCredit": [{ "name": "Example Artist", "mbid": "", "joinPhrase": "" }],
+      "events": [{ "date": "2026-09-01", "country": "XW" }],
+      "labels": [{ "name": "Example Records", "mbid": "", "catalogNumber": "EX001" }],
+      "mediums": [{
+        "format": "Digital Media",
+        "tracks": [{ "name": "Night Drive", "length": "3:41" }, { "name": "Daybreak", "length": 242000 }]
+      }],
+      "urls": ["https://example.com/night-drive"],
+      "editNote": "Details from the artist's own catalogue"
+    }
+
+``releaseGroup`` (an MBID) adds the release to an existing release group instead of creating one. ``artistCredit`` may also
+be a plain string. Track lengths are ``m:ss`` strings or milliseconds. When no ``editNote`` is given, the edit note says the
+release was seeded from Kendraio App.
+
+Example Flows
+-------------
+
+Ready-made Flows are included with the app under the ``musicbrainz`` adapter:
+
+- ``/musicbrainz/dashboard`` - links to all the Flows below
+- ``/musicbrainz/searchArtists``, ``/musicbrainz/searchReleases``, ``/musicbrainz/searchRecordings`` - search
+- ``/musicbrainz/artist?mbid=...`` - artist details and all release groups of the artist
+- ``/musicbrainz/releaseGroup?mbid=...`` - release group details and all its releases
+- ``/musicbrainz/release?mbid=...`` - release details and track list
+- ``/musicbrainz/recording?mbid=...`` - recording details and the releases it appears on
+- ``/musicbrainz/submitRelease`` - a form that prepares a release for submission to MusicBrainz
+
+Each result links to the next Flow, so you can move from an artist to its albums, to a specific edition, to a track and
+back to everything that track appears on.
+
+The same Flows are packaged as an installable adapter (``src/assets/adapters/musicbrainz.json``), listed in the app's
+built-in adapter repository. To install it, add ``/assets/adapters/`` under Settings > Adapters > Manage Repositories,
+refresh the adapter list and install MusicBrainz. This copies the Flows into the app so they can be edited, and adds
+MusicBrainz with its search and submission Flows to the services menu.
+
+MusicBrainz core data is CC0 (public domain); supplementary data such as tags, genres and annotations is available under
+CC BY-NC-SA 3.0. See https://musicbrainz.org/doc/About/Data_License
